// @corpus: platform
// @id: PLATFORM-device
// @category: platform — the device
// @charter: §7.3, §7.9
// @milestone: E5
//
// The device exists where the user is. `device.*` is granted by the browser
// world and by no other, which is what makes a geolocation read inside an
// origin-placed query a placement error (corpus R-025) rather than a runtime
// failure in production.

module device

// A point on the earth. Device-bound: it exists where the device is, which is
// what makes reading it from an origin-placed query a placement error.
//
// Declared here since 2026-09-25. It was declared in the store example's
// `examples/domain.pw` and imported from there, so every program using the
// platform package had to include the store's domain. A second application
// (the kiokun slice) was the first to notice.
type Location = Location {
    lat: Int,
    lng: Int,
}

fn current_location() -> Location !{ device.location } { todo }

fn permission_state(name: String) -> String !{ device.query } { "" }
